Summary: reviewed PR #1878 (frontend notification-channels UI). The standout bug is #1 — switching the channel Type dropdown on the "New channel" form doesn't clear stale field state from the previously-selected type, so the create payload can silently include fields for the wrong type and the backend rejects it with a confusing 422. Findings #2 and #3 are honesty/UX gaps where the frontend's copy or omitted state contradicts real backend side effects (`ChannelCredentialRedirectError` and the auth-header-name/value pairing teardown) documented directly in `channel_service.py`. #4 and #5 are minor efficiency/dead-code cleanups. All 5 were posted as inline review comments on the PR.

