`DATAQ_DB` confirmed. Here's the plan and exact queries for #1257.

## What to run in Snowflake

**Step 1 — check current state (read-only, safe):**
```sql
SHOW GRANTS TO ROLE DATAQ_LOADER;
```
Confirm you see both `MANAGE GRANTS` on the account and `OWNERSHIP` on `DATAQ_DB.ANALYTICS` / `DATAQ_DB.ANALYTICS_STG`.

**Step 2 — revoke the broad grant:**
```sql
REVOKE MANAGE GRANTS ON ACCOUNT FROM ROLE DATAQ_LOADER;
```

**Step 3 — re-run the exact six `on-run-end` grant statements as `DATAQ_LOADER`**, to prove ownership alone is sufficient (run these as/impersonating `DATAQ_LOADER`, e.g. `USE ROLE DATAQ_LOADER;` first):
```sql
USE ROLE DATAQ_LOADER;

GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA DATAQ_DB.ANALYTICS_STG TO ROLE DATAQ_READER;
GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA DATAQ_DB.ANALYTICS TO ROLE DATAQ_READER;
GRANT SELECT ON ALL VIEWS IN SCHEMA DATAQ_DB.ANALYTICS_STG TO ROLE DATAQ_READER;
GRANT SELECT ON FUTURE VIEWS IN SCHEMA DATAQ_DB.ANALYTICS_STG TO ROLE DATAQ_READER;
GRANT SELECT ON ALL DYNAMIC TABLES IN SCHEMA DATAQ_DB.ANALYTICS TO ROLE DATAQ_READER;
GRANT SELECT ON FUTURE DYNAMIC TABLES IN SCHEMA DATAQ_DB.ANALYTICS TO ROLE DATAQ_READER;
```

**If all six succeed** — `MANAGE GRANTS` is confirmed redundant, done for good, don't re-grant it.

**If any fail** — immediately re-grant as a rollback:
```sql
GRANT MANAGE GRANTS ON ACCOUNT TO ROLE DATAQ_LOADER;
```

Run these and paste me the output (or just tell me pass/fail) — I'll verify with a fresh `SHOW GRANTS TO ROLE DATAQ_LOADER` and close #1257 accordingly.
